{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MkeCTg54cLKB9X7tH2qvje","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Ticket worker: securitized-product trade capture\n2\t\n3\tBuild the complete accessible ticket component for the synthetic\n4\t`/trade-capture` workspace. Read the product brief and frozen contract first.\n5\tThe prop types are stable and domain/state logic belongs elsewhere.\n6\t\n7\tYou may change only:\n8\t\n9\t- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-ticket.tsx`\n10\t\n11\t## Required behavior\n12\t\n13\t- Render all editable `TradeDraft` fields except the internal trade ID and\n14\t  read-only allocations. Group identity, economics, product detail, and notes\n15\t  with semantic `fieldset` and `legend` elements.\n16\t- Use the frozen `tc-field-{field}` ID for every control. Labels must be\n17\t  explicitly associated with controls.\n18\t- Show each supplied exception beside its field using\n19\t  `tc-error-{field}`. Error controls use `aria-invalid`; controls with messages\n20\t  use `aria-describedby`. Warnings remain visible without marking the field\n21\t  invalid.\n22\t- Numeric inputs convert an empty string to `null`; otherwise pass a finite\n23\t  number. The component updates only through `onChange` and does not calculate\n24\t  or validate.\n25\t- Use the exact six product values, two sides, and five modifier values from\n26\t  the domain contract. Currency is visible as fixed USD.\n27\t- Provide real `type=\"button\"` actions for save draft, validate, book, and\n28\t  reset. Disable Book whenever any supplied exception has severity `error` and\n29\t  show a plain visible reason. Warnings must not disable Book.\n30\t- Preserve the existing `.tc-` class convention. Do not add inline styles,\n31\t  domain imports, state, dependencies, or network behavior.\n32\t\n33\tRun only `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint`. In the final response, report\n34\tthe changed file and check results. Do not claim browser verification.\n35\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"624754b4-6323-47dd-a059-d2daf611c27d","uuid":"ac72a405-a730-4890-9d83-9b39b1759eec","timestamp":"2026-08-23T22:20:03.410Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-jm7RJ1/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T7-trade-ticket/prompt.md","content":"# Ticket worker: securitized-product trade capture\n\nBuild the complete accessible ticket component for the synthetic\n`/trade-capture` workspace. Read the product brief and frozen contract first.\nThe prop types are stable and domain/state logic belongs elsewhere.\n\nYou may change only:\n\n- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-ticket.tsx`\n\n## Required behavior\n\n- Render all editable `TradeDraft` fields except the internal trade ID and\n  read-only allocations. Group identity, economics, product detail, and notes\n  with semantic `fieldset` and `legend` elements.\n- Use the frozen `tc-field-{field}` ID for every control. Labels must be\n  explicitly associated with controls.\n- Show each supplied exception beside its field using\n  `tc-error-{field}`. Error controls use `aria-invalid`; controls with messages\n  use `aria-describedby`. Warnings remain visible without marking the field\n  invalid.\n- Numeric inputs convert an empty string to `null`; otherwise pass a finite\n  number. The component updates only through `onChange` and does not calculate\n  or validate.\n- Use the exact six product values, two sides, and five modifier values from\n  the domain contract. Currency is visible as fixed USD.\n- Provide real `type=\"button\"` actions for save draft, validate, book, and\n  reset. Disable Book whenever any supplied exception has severity `error` and\n  show a plain visible reason. Warnings must not disable Book.\n- Preserve the existing `.tc-` class convention. Do not add inline styles,\n  domain imports, state, dependencies, or network behavior.\n\nRun only `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint`. In the final response, report\nthe changed file and check results. Do not claim browser verification.\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}}}
